    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T17:32:47Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 768fe23f0. The reproduction does not fail there without a change.\n\nEvidence:\n- I wrote an app test with the issue's document: 48-segment revolves, the blank as stock (`StockShape::FromModel`), raw stock only on, the `lathe.mch` lathe and the `TN-1600-0R8` insert.\n- The test generates Taper Turning Z40..60 (bottom diameter 18, top diameter 16, tolerance 0.05). It asserts that no `Warning::Envelope` blocks the post. Then it posts with `fanuc-lathe.cps`.\n- On the issue base `58cb641ca` the test fails with the issue's text: `finish envelope near move 7: 0.0000 mm gouge, 38.9500 mm rest`.\n- On `ec2112539` the test passes. On upstream/main `768fe23f0` the test passes and the program posts.\n- The full-cone comparison verifies and posts on all three commits.\n\nThe likely fix is `ec2112539` \"fix(turning): stop reading thread valleys and neck steps as false hidden rest\" (PR #2911, #2880). It added the recess excuse in `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_turned.rs`: a hidden top whose open recess the pass never enters is not that pass's rest. The guard tests of #2880 keep a pass that enters the recess judged.\n\nThe chamfer refusal that the issue names also does not reproduce on upstream/main with this document. The chamfer and the taper post together.\n\nSuggest closing. The maintainer decides.\n",
